---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Teaching Resources" description="Teaching resources and background material associated with Teaching and Learning Mathematics Online.">
  <header class="page-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Teaching resources</p>
      <h1>The website should be useful, too.</h1>
      <p>A book about practical online teaching ought to have a practical online companion. These resources connect the two editions and turn the site into something worth returning to after you have bought the book.</p>
    </div>
  </header>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="resource-grid">
        <article class="resource-card">
          <div class="symbol">✓</div>
          <h3>Course-design checklist</h3>
          <p>A printable preflight covering mathematical communication, interaction, assessment, technology, access, anxiety, and course structure.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/resources/course-design-checklist/">Run the checklist →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="resource-card">
          <div class="symbol">№</div>
          <h3>Chapter index</h3>
          <p>Browse all 20 first-edition and 29 second-edition chapter records, including author bylines and direct cross-edition links.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/chapters/">Browse chapters →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="resource-card">
          <div class="symbol">∑</div>
          <h3>Contributor directory</h3>
          <p>Find every published contributor and every chapter credited to that person across either edition.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/contributors/">Meet the contributors →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="resource-card">
          <div class="symbol">Δ</div>
          <h3>Edition map</h3>
          <p>See how the original 20-chapter structure became a 29-chapter second edition and where the new work entered.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/editions/">Compare editions →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="resource-card">
          <div class="symbol">“ ”</div>
          <h3>Citation records</h3>
          <p>Keep the edition, year, DOI, paperback ISBN, and eBook ISBN straight when citing the book.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/cite/">Cite TLMO →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="resource-card">
          <div class="symbol">±</div>
          <h3>Errata</h3>
          <p>The canonical home for confirmed corrections, identified by edition and chapter rather than silently changed.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/errata/">Check corrections →</a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="section-heading resource-source-heading">
        <div><p class="eyebrow">Project history</p><h2>How the editions were assembled.</h2></div>
        <p>The original project material on James Howard’s site preserves the calls for proposals and other background from the development of the books.</p>
      </div>
      <a class="button secondary" href="https://jameshoward.us/books/teaching-learning-mathematics-online/">View the project archive ↗</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
